Queue a scan against the given target with the named profile.

--profile is required; pass either the profile name (see "recon
profile list") or a UUID.

Without --watch, the command returns once the scan is queued and
prints the scan record. With --watch the command streams scan
events from /api/v1/recon/scans/<id>/events until the scan
completes or the connection drops.

Usage:
  usulnet recon scan start <target-id> [flags]

Examples:
  usulnet recon scan start 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111 --profile default
  usulnet recon scan start <target-id> --profile osint --watch

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for start
      --profile string   profile name or UUID (required)
      --watch            stream scan events to stdout

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string   config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --json            shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string   output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet           suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)
      --server string   usulnet API URL (default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --token string    API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)
